Good Afternoon,

I am trying to run a logistic regression using rjmcmc that includes a quadratic relationship between the explanatory and response variables. It seems that this should be quite simple, but I don't completely trust the way I have constructed the models. Based on what I've found in this group it looks like there are two ways to do this.

Option A is to multiply the indicator for the linear term with the indicator for the quadratic term in the model which forces the quadratic to be zero if either indicator is estimated to be zero.
example: z[1]*b[1]*X1 + z[1]*z[2]*b[2]*X1^2

Option B is to constrain the indicator for the quadratic term to be less than or equal to the indicator for the linear term.
example: constraint_data ~ dconstraint( z[2] <= z[1] )

My questions are 1) are both options considered acceptable ways to include a quadratic relationship in the model? and 2) is one option more efficient than the other?

I've attached screenshots with code for simulated examples of each option.

Thanks for your help!

Kaitlin

