Hi Kaitlin,

it seems to me that you may have already seen this conversation

https://groups.google.com/g/nimble-users/c/ROO-OMl3hlE/m/ZBXozqiCAAAJ

and that your setting is similar to the selection of covariates with interaction terms, in the sense that the quadratic term can be included in the model only if the linear one is already included.

So to answer your questions:

1) Both options are acceptable in nimble but the drawback of option A is that the regression coefficient for the quadratic term would be sampled even when it is not included in the model. This happens when z[1] = 0 and z[2] = 1. The RJ sampler with indicators works with the pairs (indicator, coefficient); in this case, we have two pairs (z[1], b[1]), (z[2], b[2]), and an indicator equal to 1 will trigger sampling of the corresponding coefficient.

2) Option B should be more efficient as it avoids the situation in 1, given that z[2] will be equal to 1 only if z[1] is equal to 1.

Hope this helps!

Sally

