Dear Kei,
The MCMC algorithm is an object that uses the model object. So the nodes with samplers in the MCMC are unrelated to whether you can calculate some or all parts of the model. The PMCMC example as given should work. That has nodes=NULL to create an empty MCMC configuration, so that the PMCMC sampler can be added to it. The PMCMC sampler (RW_PF_block) manages the x nodes using a particle filter. If you haven't had a chance, I would recommend gaining the basic concepts of nimble models and MCMC algorithms by working through the first parts of the nimble user manual at r-nimble.org <http://r-nimble.org>, looking at the examples also at r-nimble.org <http://r-nimble.org>, and also looking at some of the workshop materials available on our nimble-training GitHub organization <https://github.com/orgs/nimble-training/repositories>. The nimble-virtual-2023 and nimble-lisbon-2022 were both 3-day workshops, so they have somewhat more thorough modules than the shorter workshops.
HTH
Perry

